# Copy to web/.env.local for local development.
# On Vercel, set these in Project Settings -> Environment Variables.
#
# Note: the Python projects read the shared .env at the REPO ROOT instead.
# This file is only for the website.

# From the SoCLaaS portal. Never commit the real value — this repo is public.
SOCLAAS_API_KEY=clsk_your_key_here
SOCLAAS_BASE_URL=https://soclaas-api.comp.nus.edu.sg/v1

# The shared password for the site. Generate a long random one; it is the only
# thing standing between the open internet and your API quota:
#   node -e "console.log(crypto.randomUUID())"
APP_PASSWORD=change_me

# Signs the session cookie. Any long random string. Changing it signs everyone
# out immediately, which is how you revoke access.
#   node -e "console.log(crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
AUTH_SECRET=change_me_to_something_long_and_random

# --- Web search, OPTIONAL ----------------------------------------------------
# Set ONE of these to give Chat access to the internet. With none set, the Web
# toggle does not appear and everything else works exactly as before.
#
# Set BOTH and the chat gets a provider picker next to the Web toggle; they
# return noticeably different results, so it is worth comparing them on the same
# question. A snippet-only provider is fine -- the model reads the pages it
# picks with web_fetch.
#
#   Tavily  1,000 searches/month free, no card. Has a /usage endpoint, so the
#           sidebar counter is exact.
#   Brave   2,000/month free but needs a card on file. Publishes only a
#           per-second limit on the free plan and reports its monthly window as
#           zero, so the sidebar counter stays blank -- check Brave's own
#           dashboard instead. A paid plan does populate it.
#
# Google Programmable Search is NOT supported: closed to new customers, and
# shut down entirely on 1 January 2027.
#
# These are read at startup by web/next.config.ts -- RESTART the dev server
# after adding or changing one.

# TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-...
# BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=BSA...
